title Rule, then reading, then refusal -- the cold roster declines to open over a lap that ended at git add
prompt Autonomous loop -- roster cold first, Standfast on reds, next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, rota row N mod 5, condense ITINERARY and refill Now, send each finished increment
think Opened the roster cold before touching anything and held still for the whole twenty-one minutes, which is REDS %221's own rule applied on the first lap that had it. The reading came back staged_uncommitted=19 and 61 guards, 58 green, 3 red -- readme_metrics, geode_libraries, and nib_honesty.
think Traced all three to one root rather than treating them as three faults. tools/hooks/pre-commit regenerates README.md's metrics block and docs-geode/libraries/README.md at commit time, so a round that stops at git add leaves both describing the tree they last saw; the front door advertised 1,690 witnesses over a tree holding 1,692. nib_honesty read git_nib=absent because construction/ITINERARY.md carries the literal NIB_HERE until a commit exists whose hash replaces it. One root: the previous lap ended at git add.
think Repaired before designing. Shipped the previous round's 19 staged paths as one signed commit, let pre-commit regenerate and stage both pages inside it, read git rev-parse --short=10 HEAD, wrote it into the card's Git nib field and amended once -- which is exactly what .claude/rules/remember-git-nib.md prescribes, and what nib_honesty_scan.sh already expects under nib_local_only=yes_expected_pre_amend_sibling. All three guards GREEN, pushed to origin and xykj61 before this round's own work began.
think Then asked whether a third firing deserved a third row. REDS %188 booked this class on 20260824.082144, %220 on 20260825.092953. %188 concluded no guard can enforce the close, since such a guard would run after the lap ends -- that reasoning is sound and I left it standing. %220 answered with a reading: staged_uncommitted printed on line one. The class fired again eleven hours later, so the row is worth booking for what the recurrence teaches rather than for the incident.
think Named the ladder rather than adding a second reading. Rule, then reading, then refusal. The reading was the right diagnosis at the wrong rung, and the reason is structural: the agent that reads staged_uncommitted=19 is the one that has just arrived, so the message reaches the lap inheriting the mess rather than the lap that made it. Enforcement lives in a moment nothing runs in; measurement lands with the next reader; what remains is what a guard can decide, and it can decline to open the next lap over the wreckage.
think Placed the refusal where the reading is unambiguous, which is one moment only. A full-roster pass is how a lap opens, so staged paths at that instant belong to whoever ran last and the count carries exactly one meaning. --hot is how a round says the staged paths are its own -- the after-git-add pass REDS %174 asks for. A guard asked for by name is no lap open and passes free. One flag and one structural distinction, and I stopped there on purpose: the ales choir one room over paid for this on the same day by registering its own name rather than adding a second exemption.
think Rewrote the argument parser as a while loop so --hot composes with --all and --tier, since the cadence lap wants --hot --all and a single case statement could only read argument one. Put the refusal ahead of tree_digest and ahead of the first guard, because a pass that reports what it measured has measured nothing yet, and twenty minutes of verdicts over a tree the lap is about to change answer a different question from the one the lap has.
think Proved the refusal against the case it must leave alone, which is the half that distinguishes a guard from a blanket refusal. Inside the real git repository standing_equipment_control.sh already builds: a clean cold open runs its guard and answers ok, one staged path refuses that same pass, no guard line and no digest print above the refusal, --hot passes the same tree, a named guard runs free over it, and --hot --all still selects every tier.
think Rota row 2 by lap index. git rev-list --count HEAD read 3431 at the open and the previous lap read the same number, since that lap never committed -- so the count itself carried the red. Advanced to row 2, Air and Saturn, law and boundary: TAME_CORE, single-stranded, and GAUGE_STYLE which loads every lap anyway. Single-stranded governed the shape directly: the runner does one thing, and the refusal reads the index rather than reaching into what the lap ought to do about it.
obs The cold pass, with its conditions. 61 guards on tier lap, 58 green, 3 red, run alone on a dirty index carrying 19 staged paths, tree_moved=no across the whole pass because the round held still. Process elapsed observed at 15m36s while caravan_suite_witness ran, completing inside the following poll window, so the wall time sits between 936s and 1,226s -- consistent with the roster header's own 20m20s to 22m19s.
obs The control grew from 34 behaviors to 43, refusals bitten from nine to ten. Sixteen of the 43 now run inside a real git repository rather than a bare pen, because two of the runner's three refusals are about the repository rather than about the roster.
obs The living pin arithmetic, measured rather than estimated. REDS.md stood at 22,451 bytes and %223 as first written took it to 25,600 against the 24,576 it declares, so %221 folded to construction/archive/REDS-a-cold-roster-across-its-own-edits-rows-221.md with its link depth moved, leaving 23,512. The headline's Rows and added-under-the-law numbers moved 222/202 to 223/203, and reds_ledger_monotone caught the drift on the first run rather than a reader catching it later.
obs ITINERARY needed the same care and nearly did not get it. The two directive rewrites alone pushed the card to 24,869 over its 24,576, which equinox_e123_living_pin_guard found. Checkpoint a31664d7b6 recorded first, the ales-choir Now block condensed to a Prior-laps row, and the card reads 24,412.
obs A finding for the next lap, taken while surveying rather than assumed. The equinox family at 123 unheard is a different shape from ales: every one of them is named somewhere, and the somewhere is an almanac string its own writer prints, which the reach meter correctly reads as data rather than as a call. Twenty-one of the 144 are named by nothing at all. They are season-ceremony witnesses under tools/gen/season/, each with an idempotent almanac appender guarded by a grep, so a re-run moves no bytes -- yet whether they still pass is unmeasured, and that measurement decides whether the next lap writes a choir or classifies a closed season.
obs Graded every artifact touched. The design essay first read B+ at 89 with 44% negative sentences against Field's 30%, so it took a Gauge sweep -- nine sentences turned affirmative, every claim and every figure held exactly -- and reads A at 96 with 17%. ITINERARY A at 95, REDS A+ at 100, CHECKPOINTS A+ at 100, the new REDS shelf A+ at 100, the loop seed A+ at 100. Nothing below B, so no molt frame was pushed.
obs Owned plainly: this lap spent its first thirty minutes closing someone else's round, and that someone was the same loop. The refusal is written so the next lap spends one line on it instead.
